From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pyo <pyo@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:15:06 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat: make the name prefix of a cluster's resources
 configurable

MOCO names the resources of a MySQLCluster "moco-<name>" (StatefulSet,
Pods, Services, Secrets, ConfigMaps, backup CronJob, restore Job and
their Roles).  Add --name-prefix to moco-controller (default "moco-",
which keeps the current names) for platforms that want other names,
e.g. an empty prefix so that the Pods are "<name>-0".

The prefix is recorded in the moco.cybozu.com/name-prefix annotation
when a cluster is created (by the mutating webhook, unless the cluster
sets it) and cannot change afterwards, because the StatefulSet cannot
be renamed.  Clusters without the annotation, i.e. all existing ones,
keep "moco-".  The name length limit becomes 45 minus the prefix's
length (40 with "moco-").

The restore Job now reads the target MySQLCluster to find its Pod
instead of assuming the default name.  The Certificate and the Secret
in the controller's namespace keep their names.
