+
+## Name prefix
+
+The resources MOCO creates for a MySQLCluster are named `moco-<name>`
+(the StatefulSet, the headless Service, the ServiceAccount and the
+PodDisruptionBudget), `moco-<name>-<index>` (the Pods),
+`moco-<name>-primary` and `moco-<name>-replica` (the Services),
+`moco-<name>` and `moco-my-cnf-<name>` (the Secrets), `moco-backup-<name>`
+(the backup CronJob and its Role) and `moco-restore-<name>` (the restore
+Job and its Role).
+
+`--name-prefix` replaces `moco-` in these names for clusters created
+afterwards.  With `--name-prefix=""`, the Pods of a cluster `foo` are
+`foo-0`, `foo-1` and so on.  The prefix is recorded in the cluster's
+`moco.cybozu.com/name-prefix` annotation when it is created (a cluster
+may also set the annotation itself), and it cannot be changed later.
+Clusters without the annotation use `moco-`.
+
+The name of a MySQLCluster can be 45 characters minus the length of the
+prefix (40 with `moco-`).
+
